unit: dm-next-edit-move
commits: 4ca691697 (the move)
what: sovereign-api/src/{next_edit.rs 983, next_edit_model.rs 2462,
  next_edit_symbols.rs 714, next_edit_syntax.rs 342, next_edit_journal.rs 381}
  and src/prompts/ moved to code-next-edit (the code-intel package's tenth
  crate). routes_edit_predictions.rs STAYS in sovereign-api — its mount lives in
  server.rs::client_router_for (server.rs:161-177) and sovereign-api ->
  sovereign-daemon is a Cargo cycle (the daemon names sovereign-api,
  Cargo.toml:9) plus [[forbid]] sovereign-api -> sovereign-* with no
  sovereign-daemon except (ARCH_LAYERS.toml:711-714) — so it lands with
  server.rs at dm-daemon-api-edge. The journal outcome route splits to the host
  shell sovereign-api/src/routes_edit_predictions/outcome.rs.
  The tree-sitter registry rides a PORT: code-next-edit/src/grammar.rs declares
  Grammar + GrammarLookup, and routes_edit_predictions::grammar_for is the host
  adapter naming corpus-engine (one registry, .tsx cannot drift, ARCH 8). Shims
  in sovereign-api/src/lib.rs keep the old paths resolving; the example and the
  e2e test repoint to code_next_edit::*. DT [[module]] rows re-keyed; new rows
  for grammar.rs and outcome.rs; oversized.txt re-keys next_edit_model.rs.
  Premise correction (PROMPT §6, ralph/DECISIONS.md): the row's shell
  destination and consumer list were stale, and src/prompts/ had to move with
  next_edit_model.rs. Two fan-ins hand-raised with a SYSTEM_OVERVIEW.md §10.1ad
  ledger (corpus-engine-scip 10 -> 11, sovereign-contracts 32 -> 33;
  --update-baseline not run).
checks: CLEAN exit=0; LINT exit=0 (WORKSPACE, errors: 0); LAYER exit=0
  ("fan-in within caps"); BOUNDARY exit=0 (code-intel 6/6 crates present);
  TOML exit=0; CENSUS exit=0 (11/11 positives caught, 11/11 negatives refused);
  TEST(code-next-edit) exit=0 (75 pass, 0 fail); TEST(sovereign-api) exit=0
